1
00:00:04,814 --> 00:00:07,487
Whiskers and the Loch Ness Secret.

2
00:00:15,871 --> 00:00:20,199
One spring morning, Whiskers ate the last shortbread in the tin.

3
00:00:23,287 --> 00:00:25,800
Gone. All gone. Life is over.

4
00:00:26,000 --> 00:00:27,989
Wait! There's writing inside the lid!

5
00:00:28,189 --> 00:00:31,847
Photograph the Loch Ness Monster, and win shortbread for life!

6
00:00:32,047 --> 00:00:33,828
Shortbread. For. Life.

7
00:00:34,028 --> 00:00:36,737
Loch Ness is in Scotland, far to the north.

8
00:00:41,270 --> 00:00:44,658
The wild geese are flying north! Pip, lend us your camera!

9
00:00:44,858 --> 00:00:46,758
Take care of it. And of each other!

10
00:00:56,104 --> 00:00:59,802
So the cats hitched a ride north, with the wild geese.

11
00:01:00,002 --> 00:01:02,871
Could we fly a little lower? Or not at all?

12
00:01:07,403 --> 00:01:11,103
At dawn, a sea fog called the haar covered Edinburgh.

13
00:01:22,856 --> 00:01:25,551
Look! A castle, on top of a giant rock!

14
00:01:32,972 --> 00:01:36,466
Och, hello! I'm Dougal. Welcome to the Royal Mile!

15
00:01:36,666 --> 00:01:38,639
We're looking for the Loch Ness Monster!

16
00:01:38,839 --> 00:01:41,947
Nessie? Nobody ever finds her. She's very shy.

17
00:01:42,147 --> 00:01:44,923
I just need one photo. And a snack.

18
00:01:45,123 --> 00:01:47,934
Then try some tablet. Pure Scottish sugar!

19
00:01:59,688 --> 00:02:02,719
I'm perfectly calm! Race you to the castle!

20
00:02:11,584 --> 00:02:14,696
Edinburgh Castle! It sits on an old volcano.

21
00:02:14,896 --> 00:02:17,516
A volcano? Does it ever go boom?

22
00:02:17,716 --> 00:02:20,371
No, no. It's perfectly quiet up here.

23
00:02:28,274 --> 00:02:31,509
Except for the One O'Clock Gun. Every single day.

24
00:02:31,709 --> 00:02:34,557
I jumped on purpose. For a better view.

25
00:02:42,941 --> 00:02:46,313
This is Greyfriars Bobby. A wee dog, just like me.

26
00:02:46,513 --> 00:02:50,315
When his master died, Bobby stayed by him for fourteen years.

27
00:02:50,515 --> 00:02:52,055
That's what a true friend does.

28
00:02:52,255 --> 00:02:54,848
I can't even wait fourteen minutes for lunch.

29
00:02:55,048 --> 00:02:57,773
Nessie only shows herself to those who wait.

30
00:03:09,045 --> 00:03:13,232
In the Highlands, the hills were purple with heather, and very big.

31
00:03:17,764 --> 00:03:20,624
Who's there? I can't see a thing through my fringe.

32
00:03:20,824 --> 00:03:23,044
Are you Hamish? We're going to Loch Ness!

33
00:03:23,244 --> 00:03:26,711
Hop on, wee ones. It's a slow ride, but a sure one.

34
00:03:33,651 --> 00:03:36,061
Hamish, left! No, your other left!

35
00:03:44,926 --> 00:03:48,834
At last, Loch Ness. Deep, and dark, and very still.

36
00:03:49,034 --> 00:03:51,086
Come out, monster. Smile!

37
00:03:57,063 --> 00:03:59,710
This is taking forever. Nap time.

38
00:04:05,687 --> 00:04:08,461
Bobby waited fourteen years. I can wait one night.

39
00:04:18,289 --> 00:04:21,078
Hello? Are you the ones who waited for me?

40
00:04:21,278 --> 00:04:22,862
Whiskers! Wake up! It's her!

41
00:04:26,913 --> 00:04:30,724
A camera! Please don't. People would come with boats and nets.

42
00:04:30,924 --> 00:04:33,154
I would never have peace again.

43
00:04:40,093 --> 00:04:41,641
Shortbread for life...

44
00:04:45,693 --> 00:04:49,759
No. A friend is better than shortbread. Your secret is safe.

45
00:04:49,959 --> 00:04:52,778
You would do that for me? Then climb aboard!

46
00:05:02,605 --> 00:05:04,482
We're riding the Loch Ness Monster!

47
00:05:04,682 --> 00:05:06,472
And nobody will ever know.

48
00:05:18,225 --> 00:05:20,851
You're home! Did you find the Loch Ness Monster?

49
00:05:21,051 --> 00:05:24,011
Monster? What monster? There's no monster.

50
00:05:24,211 --> 00:05:25,753
We only took one picture.

51
00:05:29,804 --> 00:05:31,985
That's just a funny rock behind you.

52
00:05:32,185 --> 00:05:34,088
Exactly. Just a rock.

53
00:05:37,658 --> 00:05:43,247
Because a loyal friend keeps your secret. Even for all the shortbread in Scotland.

